 "lemmaTab": null,
 "introduction":
 "The product type comes with function of type `A × B → B × A` which swaps the elements of an ordered pair.\n\nThis function can be defined by using the elimination rule for product types to map out of `A × B` followed by the introduction rule for product types to map into `B × A`.\n\nThe swap function can be defined by introducing a variable `p : A × B`, projecting to its components `p.1 : A` and `p.2 : B`, then reassembling these to give an element of type `B × A`.\n\nCan you define this function?",
 "index": 4,
 "image": "",
 "displayName": null,
 "descrText":
 "Product types are symmetric: an element of type `A × B` has a corresponding element of type `B × A` with components swapped.",
 "descrFormat": "example {A B : Type} : A × B → B × A  := by",
